9. PERIODIC BACKGROUND VALIDATION OF MANUAL ARTWORK URLS

Implement a server-side background validation system that periodically checks all manually mapped artwork URLs and identifies broken links.

This must be a real maintenance system, not just a dashboard display.

A. Scheduled validation

Validate manually mapped artwork URLs from the existing manual mapping registry, including:

- `src/utils/ManualWikiMapping.ts`
- `server/manualCardMappings.ts`
- Any other authoritative manual artwork mapping source

The validation system must:

- Periodically check every manually mapped direct artwork URL.
- Use HTTP `HEAD` requests where supported.
- Fall back to lightweight `GET` requests if `HEAD` is unsupported or unreliable.
- Avoid downloading or storing entire artwork files.
- Follow redirects.
- Record the final destination URL.
- Validate Wiki title-based mappings through the Wiki API separately when applicable.
- Use request timeouts.
- Use bounded retries.
- Respect rate limits.
- Use controlled concurrency.
- Prevent duplicate validation jobs from running simultaneously.

Do not use a frontend timer or browser-based process as the scheduler.

The scheduled task must be implemented through a reliable server-side scheduler compatible with the actual hosting architecture.

If Cloud Run does not support reliable scheduled execution within the current configuration, use a compatible scheduling mechanism such as an external scheduler calling a secured server endpoint.

Do not claim that background scheduling works unless the required scheduler is actually configured.

B. Validation statuses

Each mapping must support the following statuses:

- `healthy` — successfully verified
- `broken` — confirmed permanent failure
- `redirected` — redirected to another valid location
- `unverified` — not checked yet
- `temporarily_unavailable` — timeout, network failure, rate limit, or temporary server error

Record:

- Card ID
- Card name
- Card number
- Set code
- Mapping type
- Original URL
- Wiki title or filename
- Validation status
- HTTP status code
- Final URL
- Last checked timestamp
- Last successful validation timestamp
- Consecutive confirmed failures
- Failure reason

Store validation information separately from the original artwork mapping.

Never automatically delete or overwrite a manual artwork mapping because its validation failed.

Temporary failures must not be classified as permanently broken.

C. Admin dashboard for artwork validation

Integrate validation results into the existing admin interface.

